# System Architecture & Technical Deep-Dive: Sky Events & SFx

## System Overview & Tech Stack Breakdown

**Sky Events & SFx** (`sky-events-sfx`) is an event special-effects booking and administration Single-Page Application (SPA) designed as an academic mini-project (MCA Sem-III, Course ITP31). The application handles customer bookings for stage pyrotechnics, entrance special effects, confetti showers, and ambient atmospheric fog, along with customer account management, testimonials moderation, general enquiries, and an administrator control panel.

### Tech Stack Specifications

| Layer | Technology / Library | Purpose & Rationale |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Core Framework** | Vanilla HTML5 & ES6 JavaScript (Modules) | Lightweight Single-Page Application with native browser hash routing (`window.location.hash`). |
| **Styling & Design** | Vanilla CSS3 + Glassmorphism Aesthetics | Custom dark-themed visual design (`style.css`) using CSS variables, flexbox/grid, backdrop blurs, and CSS keyframe animations. |
| **Build & Dev Server** | Vite `^4.5.3` | Hot Module Replacement (HMR) local dev server, production asset bundling, and static serving. |
| **Typography & Icons** | Google Fonts (Outfit & Inter), FontAwesome `v6.4.0` | Custom typography hierarchy and icon set loaded via CDN. |
| **Data & Storage** | Browser `localStorage` & `sessionStorage` | Simulated relational database (seed data, users, bookings, services, gallery, enquiries, testimonials) and active session state storage. |

