## Technical Debt, Security Risks & Key Improvement Areas

> [!WARNING]
> ### 1. Client-Side Security & Plaintext Authentication
> - **Plaintext Credentials**: Passwords (`passwordHash`) are stored directly as unhashed plaintext inside `localStorage`.
> - **Client-Side Auth Guard Bypass**: Session state lives entirely in `sessionStorage` without server-side JWT or HTTP-only cookies. Anyone can manipulate `sessionStorage.setItem('sky_session', ...)` in DevTools to gain admin access.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### 2. Monolithic Application Structure
> - **Single File Logic**: All business logic, DOM manipulation, state management, HTML generation, and seed data reside in one 1,815-line file ([app.js](file:///d:/anti%20sky/app.js)).
> - **Lack of Component Modularization**: UI views are manually constructed via string concatenation (`innerHTML = ...`), making rendering vulnerable to XSS if input sanitization is missed.

> [!NOTE]
> ### 3. Tooling & Testing Gaps
> - **Zero Test Coverage**: No unit test suite (e.g. Vitest/Jest) or end-to-end suite (Cypress/Playwright) is configured.
> - **Missing Linter / Formatter**: No ESLint or Prettier setup in `package.json`.

